From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nixpkgs-netbsd <noreply@example.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gcc: netbsd: use PIE_SPEC for crtbegin/crtend selection

With --enable-default-pie the driver passes -pie to the linker via
LINK_PIE_SPEC, but that never sets the `pie` spec variable, so
%{pie:crtbeginS%O%s} did not match and the non-PIC crtbegin.o/crtend.o
(built with -fno-PIE) were linked into PIE executables, breaking the
first executable link of every target library configure (libatomic):

  ld.bfd: crtbegin.o: relocation R_X86_64_32 against hidden symbol
          TMC_END can not be used when making a PIE object

Use the PIE_SPEC macro (as gnu-user.h does), which expands to "!no-pie"
under --enable-default-pie and to "pie" otherwise.
---
--- a/gcc/config/netbsd-elf.h	2026-10-01 16:46:47.934810700 +0300
+++ b/gcc/config/netbsd-elf.h	2026-10-01 16:50:50.619750509 +0300
@@ -41,9 +41,8 @@
    %:if-exists(crti%O%s)	\
    %{static:%:if-exists-else(crtbeginT%O%s crtbegin%O%s)} \
    %{!static:                   \
-     %{!shared:                 \
-       %{!pie:crtbegin%O%s}     \
-       %{pie:crtbeginS%O%s}}    \
+     %{!shared:                 %{"\
+ PIE_SPEC ":crtbeginS%O%s;:crtbegin%O%s}}    \
      %{shared:crtbeginS%O%s}}"
 
 #undef STARTFILE_SPEC
@@ -55,9 +54,8 @@
    C++ file-scope static objects deconstructed after exiting "main".  */
 
 #define NETBSD_ENDFILE_SPEC	\
-  "%{!shared:                   \
-    %{!pie:crtend%O%s}          \
-    %{pie:crtendS%O%s}}         \
+  "%{!shared:                   %{"\
+ PIE_SPEC ":crtendS%O%s;:crtend%O%s}}         \
    %{shared:crtendS%O%s}        \
    %:if-exists(crtn%O%s)"
 
